The other night, I dreamed I was playing Nethack 3.1 - a curious
dream indeed.  It seemed much like the nethack I know, until I
stumbled upon an accessory I had never heard of:

G - a salt shaker

I decided to use a scroll of identify to get more information:

G - an uncursed salt shaker (12)

Interesting... the thing had "charges" of some sort, and indeed
a scroll of charging would replenish it.  Now I figured that I
should try it, so i "a"pplied it.  The message was:

What would you like to salt? [h-k, or ?*]

Well, the suggested items were all food items, so I salted a food
ration.  Didn't seem to make any difference when I ate the food,
it was only after I had done a few that I noticed that salted food
was never "rotten".

I decided that the next thing to try was salting a corpse!
I found that salted corpses didn't taste as bad.  They also took
twice as long to spoil and rot away.  I could take advantage of
this in several ways: cockatrice corpses could be wielded twice
as long, I could drag corpses to an altar from a further distance,
and I could postpone eating corpses a little longer if needed.

I tried salting other things besides food items.  Not much happened
until I salted some water.  Then I had:

J - a potion of salt water

This stuff had several uses.  I could drink it to cure hallucinogenation,
or to make me vomit up tainted food.  I could throw it (in any direction)
if I were swallowed by a monster, and the monster would regurgitate me.

I also tried wielding the salt shaker.  When I tried to hit a monster
the message was like:

You shake salt on the orc -more-

This didn't seem to bother most monsters, except the salt was deadly
to gelatinous cubes!

Cursing the salt shaker made the salt clog, so it wouldn't work very
well.  Blessing it gave it a 50-50 chance of not using up a salt
"charge" when applied.


Another curious thing happened.  I came across a gray stone.  I
carefully kicked it, and when it skidded across the room, I
rejoiced that I had a luckstone, and I picked it up.
Sometime later, when I quaffed a potion of enlightenment, I
noticed that my luck was unaffected!

Curious now, I used a scroll of identify on the stone:

Q - an uncursed dhrystone

What a dream!
